{
  "company_name": "NucleoSafe Systems",
  "industry": "Power Generation",
  "use_case": "Nuclear reactor safety monitoring and compliance tracking",
  "space_title": "NucleoSafe Systems - Nuclear Safety & Compliance ☢️",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Power Generation\n\n**Use case:** Nuclear Reactor Safety & Compliance\n\nNucleoSafe Systems — reactor safety and NRC compliance analytics across 20 components spanning fuel assemblies, control rods, coolant pumps, steam generators, and containment. Reactor Engineers and Operations Managers use this space to monitor neutron flux, coolant flow, and containment pressure; NRC Compliance teams use it to track inspection findings, deficiencies, and corrective actions against INPO performance indicators.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- NRC compliance score — INPO benchmark; Index 1 plants score >95\n- Safety margin (%) — distance to operating limit; >20% acceptable\n- Total alarm count — safety-system event frequency\n- Open corrective actions — backlog vs. NRC commitments\n- Deficiency count per inspection — quality trend indicator\n- Forced outage rate (nuclear) — target <2% (vs ~5% fleet thermal)\n- Days since last inspection — surveillance interval compliance\n- Component health distribution — Normal / Watch / Warning / Critical\n\n**Data sources**\n- `reactor_components` — daily temperature, pressure, radiation, health status per component\n- `safety_readings` — neutron flux, coolant flow, containment pressure, alarm counts\n- `inspection_snapshots` — periodic NRC compliance scores, deficiencies, corrective actions",
  "schema_basename": "nuclear_safety",
  "tables": [
