  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports nuclear reactor safety monitoring and NRC compliance for a 20-component fleet across two reactor units. Personas: Reactor Engineer (neutron_flux_pct, coolant_flow_rate_m3h, containment_pressure_kpa), Operations Manager (health_status, alarm_count, safety_margin_pct), and NRC Compliance lead (compliance_score, deficiency_count, corrective_actions_open).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- NRC compliance score = compliance_score; INPO Index 1 (top quartile) plants score >95; <80 triggers regulatory action.\n- Safety margin = safety_margin_pct; distance to safety limit; >20% acceptable, <10% requires action.\n- Neutron flux = neutron_flux_pct of rated; normal operation 90-100% at full power; deviations indicate reactivity transients.\n- Coolant flow = coolant_flow_rate_m3h; PWR primary loop typically 5,000-20,000 m³/h; low flow triggers Tech Spec entry.\n- Containment pressure = containment_pressure_kpa; design pressure ~100-110 kPa; deviation indicates leak path.\n- Health status: Normal / Watch / Warning / Critical — Warning+ triggers work-order generation.\n- Inspection result: Pass / Conditional Pass / Fail / Deferred; Fail rate target <1%.\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - safety_kpi_monthly (source: safety_readings) — dims: reading_date, component_type, reactor_unit; measures: avg_neutron_flux_pct, avg_coolant_flow_rate, total_alarm_count, avg_safety_margin, reading_count, total_containment_pressure_kpa, unique_component_count, max_neutron_flux_percent.\n  - inspection_kpi_monthly (source: inspection_snapshots) — dims: inspection_date, component_type, reactor_unit, inspection_result; measures: avg_compliance_score, total_deficiencies, total_open_corrective_actions, inspection_count, fail_count, unique_component_count, max_compliance_score, total_days_since_last_inspection.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. component_id, component_name, temperature_celsius, pressure_mpa, radiation_msv, health_status, days_since_last_inspection).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly average NRC compliance score by reactor unit for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Top 10 components by total deficiencies found this year.",
    "Which component types had the most failed inspections this year, and how many corrective actions remain open?",
    "How has total safety alarm count trended month-over-month by component type?",
    "Which components currently sit in Warning or Critical health status, and what is their average safety margin?",
    "Top 10 components by days since last inspection — are any past the 90-day surveillance window?",
    "What is the monthly trend in average safety margin percentage across the reactor fleet?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest neutron flux percent?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(max_neutron_flux_percent) AS max_neutron_flux_percent",
        "FROM {fqn}.safety_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total safety alarms triggered changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(total_alarm_count) AS total_alarm_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.safety_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique components?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT inspection_date, MEASURE(unique_component_count) AS unique_component_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.inspection_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY inspection_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does fail count vary across component types?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT component_type, MEASURE(fail_count) AS fail_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.inspection_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY fail_count DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does total component temperature in celsius break down by reactor component identifier for 'Critical' records?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT component_id, COUNT(*) AS record_count, SUM(temperature_celsius) AS total_temperature_celsius",
        "FROM {fqn}.reactor_components",
        "WHERE health_status = 'Critical' GROUP BY component_id ORDER BY total_temperature_celsius DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total containment pressure in kilopascals over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, SUM(containment_pressure_kpa) AS total_containment_pressure_kpa",
        "FROM {fqn}.safety_readings",
        "GROUP BY reading_date ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average nrc compliance score 0-100 changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT inspection_date, AVG(compliance_score) AS avg_compliance_score",
        "FROM {fqn}.inspection_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY inspection_date ORDER BY inspection_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sql_snippets": {
    "filters": [
